topic    grants
summary  what a program is given, and how to give it more
---
A program reaches only what it is given. Naming a file on a command's line gives it that
file, with the access its description asks for; +r PATH (read) and +w PATH (read and
write) before the command give it a directory or file more.

  grants cp notes.txt project/notes.txt     what cp would get, without running it

Until TASK-18 step 7 the file commands are built into the shell and programs get the
console and their own job, and nothing of the files: grants says so.

